 "captions": {
  "1": [
   "Both finger tags and a 20 mm target 60 mm past the tips in one picture, all found by the AprilTag detector.",
   "Simulated from the CAD: fingers 40 mm apart, f/8, focused 108 mm out. The target is 225 px across."
  ],
  "2": [
   "Even at 8 mm the fingers are out of the picture: the zoom's front is 39 mm further forward, and it sees 43 degrees across, not 55.",
   "The target no longer fits past 12 mm, and from 32 mm the zoom can't focus that close. It's also 2.8 times heavier, and cuts into the bracket."
  ],
  "3": [
   "Moving the lens from 400 to 108 mm does what zooming would: 5 to 18 px/mm, and into the 6 mm's sharpest distance.",
   "Nothing on the camera changes, so its one calibration still holds, and the fingers stay in view."
  ]
 },
